<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0704</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.1068</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0378</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0471</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0786</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.1186</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0430</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0531</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0658</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0976</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.13" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0358</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.8.1.17.14" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.8.1.17.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0439</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel">
<li id="S5.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">*</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Methods reproduced with authors’ official implementations/configs when available.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CaMRec</span> on the Amazon <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baby</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sports</span>, and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clothing</span> datasets using the leave-one-out protocol, reporting <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recall@10/20</span> and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NDCG@10/20</span>. <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CaMRec</span> was compared with CF baselines such as BPR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rendle et al., 2009</a>)</cite> and LightGCN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2020c</a>)</cite>, and several multimodal methods including VBPR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">He and McAuley, 2016</a>)</cite>, MMGCN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, GRCN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, DualGNN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, SLMRec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tao et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, LATTICE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, FREEDOM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou and Shen, 2023</a>)</cite>, BM3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and recent works such as DiffMM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>, DA-MRS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xv et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, M3CSR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and FETTLE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1. Performance Comparison with State-of-the-Art Methods ‣ 5. Experiment ‣ Causal Inspired Multi Modal Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CaMRec</span> outperforms strong baselines across datasets and metrics, with an average improvement of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.01%</span> over the best baseline, and a maximum gain of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7.71%</span> in NDCG@20 on the <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sports</span> dataset. Ablation studies (omitted for space) indicate that removing either the diffusion-based confounder extractor or causal subgraph reconstruction results in up to a 5% drop in performance, highlighting the importance of both backdoor and frontdoor adjustments. Visualizations of environment clusters and pruned graphs further demonstrate <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CaMRec</span>’s interpretability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the effectiveness of key components in our proposed <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CaMRec</span> framework, we conduct comprehensive ablation studies on the Amazon <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baby</span> dataset. We design three variant models:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o Backdoor</span>: Removes the back-door adjustment module, including the dual-channel cross-modal diffusion and environment codebook.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o Frontdoor</span>: Removes the front-door adjustment module, including the causal topology reconstruction.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o DCD</span>: Removes only the Dual-Channel Diffusion component while retaining the environment codebook.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2. </span>Ablation study results on Amazon <span id="S5.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baby</span> dataset</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T2.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T2.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variant</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R@10</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R@20</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NDCG@10</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.4.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NDCG@20</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">w/o Backdoor</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.0644</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.0984</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.0352</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.0439</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">w/o Frontdoor</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0667</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1018</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0354</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0443</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">w/o DCD</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0655</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0993</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0356</td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.0440</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.4.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.4.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full CaMRec</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.4.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0704</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.4.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.1068</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.4.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0378</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.4.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.4.5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0471</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2. Ablation Study ‣ 5. Experiment ‣ Causal Inspired Multi Modal Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we observe that:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Both causal adjustments are crucial.</span> Removing either back-door or front-door adjustment leads to significant performance degradation. The back-door adjustment appears to have a more substantial impact, with performance drops of 8.5% in R@10 and 7.1% in NDCG@20 when removed, suggesting that modal confounding poses a more critical challenge in multimodal recommendation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Dual-Channel Diffusion is essential.</span> The w/o DCD variant shows intermediate performance degradation, indicating that the diffusion-based confounder extraction plays a vital role in accurately identifying modal confounders. The performance drop (7.0% in R@10) demonstrates that simple environment stratification without proper confounder estimation is insufficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3) Component complementarity.</span> The full model achieves the best performance, confirming that back-door and front-door adjustments address complementary aspects of bias in multimodal recommendation systems.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.acknowledgements1" class="ltx_acknowledgements">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_acknowledgements">Acknowledgements.</h6>
To Robert, for the bagels and explaining CMYK and color spaces.

</div>
</section>
</section>
